========================================================================================
LEG 1  SPECTRAL REDUCTION: char_A(T1|>T2)=char_A(T1)*char_A(T2); spec(T)=U spec(SCC)
========================================================================================
iso classes: {3: 2, 4: 4, 5: 12, 6: 56}
  (a) eig(T1|>T2) == eig(T1) U eig(T2) for all n=3 x n=3 joins:  max err = 0.00e+00
  (b) char_A(T) == prod char_A(strong components), EXACT over all 74 classes n<=6:  mismatches = 0
  => the SPECTRAL atoms are the strongly-connected tournaments (block-triangular reducibility).
     [numpy float eigvals err ~sqrt(3) on nilpotent transitive blocks is ill-conditioning, not a real gap]

========================================================================================
LEG 2  SINE-PRODUCT: Sum_T (-1)^{back} x^{score} = prod(x_j-x_i) = product of sines on circle
========================================================================================
  n=3  |Sum_T(-1)^back x^score - prod(x_j-x_i)| = 4.44e-16
  n=4  |Sum_T(-1)^back x^score - prod(x_j-x_i)| = 8.62e-15
  n=5  |Sum_T(-1)^back x^score - prod(x_j-x_i)| = 2.21e-13
  circle n=5: |signed_partition(e^{i th}) - prod 2i sin((th_j-th_i)/2) e^{i(th_i+th_j)/2}| = 4.28e-14
  roots of unity n=5: |prod(w^j - w^i)| = 55.9017   (n^{n/2} = 55.9017)  [=sqrt|disc(x^n-1)|]
  roots of unity n=7: |prod(w^j - w^i)| = 907.4927   (n^{n/2} = 907.4927)  [=sqrt|disc(x^n-1)|]

========================================================================================
LEG 3  TRIGONOMETRIC ATOMS: circulant tournament eigenvalues as explicit trig sums
========================================================================================
  Paley-7: Re(eigenvalues) = [-0.5, 3.0] ; Gauss-sum Re for j!=0 = [-0.5]  (theory: -0.5)
  Paley-11: Re(eigenvalues) = [-0.5, 5.0] ; Gauss-sum Re for j!=0 = [-0.5]  (theory: -0.5)
  Paley-19: Re(eigenvalues) = [-0.5, 9.0] ; Gauss-sum Re for j!=0 = [-0.5]  (theory: -0.5)
  interval C={1..3} n=7 (tournament=True): Re(lam_j) == (Dirichlet_3(2pi j/n)-1)/2 ? True
  interval C={1..4} n=9 (tournament=True): Re(lam_j) == (Dirichlet_4(2pi j/n)-1)/2 ? True
  interval C={1..5} n=11 (tournament=True): Re(lam_j) == (Dirichlet_5(2pi j/n)-1)/2 ? True

  => circulant atoms' eigenvalues are Gauss sums (Paley) / Dirichlet-kernel values (interval);
     via LEG 1 the spectrum of ANY reducible tournament is built from these trig atoms.
